## Context

`erg new` was fixed in 0166 to reject unknown `-`-prefixed flags instead of
silently treating them as the DIR positional (footgun: typo → stray directory).
The fix established the house convention in rm.go/new.go: iterate args, switch
over known flags, reject unknowns with a usage message.

A celebrate sweep found the same pre-fix pattern in 5 more commands that do
raw `args[N]` indexing with no flag guard:

- `src/go/check.go` — `args[0]` as explicit dir
- `src/go/close.go` — `args[0]` id/file, `args[1]` reason
- `src/go/log.go`   — `args[0]` id, `args[1]` line
- `src/go/label.go` — `args[0]` id, `args[1]` label (add + remove)
- `src/go/init.go`  — `args[0]` as root dir

A typo on any of these (e.g. `erg close 0042 --resson "typo"`) silently
passes `--resson` as the reason string rather than erroring. For mutating
commands this can produce garbage ticket content.

## Actions

For each of the 5 files, add the flag-rejection guard following the
rm.go/new.go pattern:
1. Iterate args with an index loop
2. Switch: known flags handled, unknown `-`-prefixed tokens → error + usage,
   everything else → positional slice
3. Replace `args[N]` references with `positional[N]`
4. Update usage strings / helptext to document any flags

## Relevant files

- `src/go/check.go`, `close.go`, `log.go`, `label.go`, `init.go`
- `src/go/rm.go`, `src/go/new.go` — reference implementations

## Exit criteria

- [ ] All 5 commands reject unknown `-`-prefixed tokens with a non-zero exit
      and a usage message
- [ ] Positional behavior (existing tests) unchanged — `make check` passes
- [ ] Shell integration tests cover the unknown-flag rejection for each command
